 "response": "Tepi's budget is now **$2022K**. Two rules from the policy decide which records count:\n- **Only Finance Office records count.** Messages from Sales, Legal, Operations and others are ignored, as are Finance Office notes that don't change the budget (audits, receipts, invoice batches and the like).\n- **Withdrawals can be withdrawn.** For each chain, I worked from the last withdrawal backwards. A withdrawal that is itself withdrawn has no effect, so the update it targeted stands again.\n\n**How the main chains resolve:**\n- #0002 is withdrawn. The chain is #1545 \u2192 #0504 \u2192 #0031 \u2192 #0018 \u2192 #0005, so #0005's withdrawal of #0002 holds.\n- #0035 stands. Its chain runs from #0920 down to #0069, and the final effective step undoes the withdrawal of #0035.\n- #0011, #0036, #0027 and #0091 stand, because the withdrawals against them were themselves withdrawn.\n- #0066, #0138, #0029, #0085, #0480, #0750, #0260 and #0808 are withdrawn, because their withdrawal chains end on an effective withdrawal.\n- 112 budget updates are withdrawn in total, including #0002 and #0008.\n\n**Calculation:** The budget starts at $1810K from #0001. I then applied every remaining Finance Office increase and decrease in record order, skipping the withdrawn ones. That gives a final total of $2022K. With this many records, a slip in the running sum is possible.\n\nANSWER: $2022K",
